{"title":"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a trapezoid, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6e9606f5f5145fa67e77691d5781cf36f118ccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79d59606e95a672417b3f91d8f28607ddf92e475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 50$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3df80c6052a2128b30eb8a39a49d8ed45409800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 20$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, and the altitude is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of the trapezoid?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bd7719b521c33191726670908546d54161aeda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D; A=(3,20); B=(35,20); C=(47,0); D=(0,0); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); dot((0,0)); dot((3,20)); dot((35,20)); dot((47,0)); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,S); draw((19,20)--(19,0)); dot((19,20)); dot((19,0)); draw((19,3)--(22,3)--(22,0)); label(&quot;12&quot;,(21,10),E); label(&quot;50&quot;,(19,22),N); label(&quot;15&quot;,(1,10),W); label(&quot;20&quot;,(41,12),E);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"148\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece09600bac75b839d79a2665b3d55b3beb25580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }600\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }650\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }700\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }750\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }800$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde7b3b44e3f5ba857b5151d425928901478ec30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1.5mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.9pt)+fontsize(10pt)); dotfactor=3;  pair A,B,C,D,X,Y; A=(9,12); B=(59,12); C=(75,0); D=(0,0); X=(9,0); Y=(59,0); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(A--X); draw(B--Y);  pair[] ps={A,B,C,D,X,Y}; dot(ps);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,SE); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y,S); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,D--X,S); label(&quot;$b$&quot;,Y--C,S); label(&quot;$15$&quot;,D--A,NW); label(&quot;$50$&quot;,B--A,N); label(&quot;$20$&quot;,B--C,NE); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,X--A,E); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,Y--B,W); [/asy]\" width=\"572\" height=\"122\" />\n</p><p>If you draw altitudes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc7892b9acc4ec136a9946aadb6c0f15ff1ed41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> the trapezoid will be divided into two right triangles and a rectangle. You can find the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> with the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a>.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/2755d6e1e591261df5a6462b4497b28773090c56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=\\sqrt{15^2-12^2}=\\sqrt{81}=9\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6556edf7ce29e6cdbce56c0514b89382528d87.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b=\\sqrt{20^2-12^2}=\\sqrt{256}=16\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e6489c5f28baa4bd02a233c02d29792f17e4b11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABYX$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a rectangle so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356a5f06e0a855005ed2b04d06883932d7053a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=AB=50.$\" width=\"129\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/9843a0050be4143ca4e871f1cef98b398ac84e66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CD=a+XY+b=9+50+16=75\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The area of the trapezoid is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/5/83558d77c0d5b33f316ba373de8af2f83e88e8dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12\\cdot \\frac{(50+75)}{2} = 6(125) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 750}\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/51K3uCzntWs?t=2521\">https://youtu.be/51K3uCzntWs?t=2521</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MjxiQ9MZiHk\">https://youtu.be/MjxiQ9MZiHk</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 8\">2011 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/